# Retarget architecture rules

The public model is **typed-first and enum-free**. There are no identifier enums
(`MarkerId`, `SegmentId`, `PatchId`, `SubjectId`, `TrackId`) and no `NameId`.
Authored string names are identity.

## Dual-purpose schema dataclasses

`Marker`, `Patch`, `Segment[MarkersT, PatchesT]`, and `Subject[SegmentsT]` are
frozen, slotted dataclasses that serve as **both** the authoring values and the
bound runtime query surface. They carry a private, non-init `_binding`
(`field(default=None, init=False, compare=False, repr=False)`) that links them to
loaded data. It is `None` while authoring and excluded from equality/repr.

Do not split these back into `SegmentSpec` + `SegmentView` + handles. Do not add
`SubjectId`/`MarkerId`/etc. Do not put runtime binding in the public constructor.

## TypedDict schema bases

`Markers`, `Patches`, `Segments`, `Subjects` (core) and `Tracks` (demo) are
`TypedDict` bases. Concrete subclasses give the deep query chain its static
typing, because concrete `TypedDict`s project literal keys to declared types.

## Deep-chain typing is load-bearing

```python
demo.tracks["mocap"]                          # MocapTrack[SubjectsT]
mocap.subjects["left_shoe"].segments["shoe"]  # Segment[...]
segment.markers["heel"].positions()           # TimeVec3
```

This works via `Demonstration[TracksT].tracks -> TracksT` and
`MocapTrack[SubjectsT].subjects -> SubjectsT`. Do not regress it and do not add
codegen.

## Targets, keys, state

Stable runtime keys are string-based dataclasses:

```python
SegmentTarget(subject, segment)
MarkerTarget(subject, segment, marker)
PatchTarget(subject, segment, patch)
SegmentKey(subject, segment)
```

`SceneState.segment_poses` is keyed by `SegmentKey` (strings). `ContactTrack`
keys off `PatchTarget`. `SceneState`/`SegmentPoseTrajectory` remain the internal
pose store; `SegmentPoseTrajectory` may be empty (materialized empty slices).

Do not reintroduce `MarkerHandle`/`PatchHandle` or enum-typed identity.

## build_scene and loading

`build_scene(subjects)` path-binds the authored schema (targets + geometry
available, no time-series) and returns the same `SubjectsT`. `load_mocap_track`
returns a `MocapTrack[SubjectsT]` whose `.subjects` answers time-series queries.
`calibrate_patch_transform(...)` is the backend helper that fits a patch frame
from segment-frame marker positions (apply `marker_translations` before fitting,
`normal_offset` after).

## IO

IO parses raw JSON/VSK and exposes typed values. `load_scene_state`,
`load_mocap_track`, and `marker_position` take authored string names; do not
reintroduce enum/spec-typed IO signatures.

## Type style

Use PEP 695 generics with defaults. Use `Mapping` for inputs and
`MappingProxyType` for stored immutable mappings. Keep `py.typed`. Concrete
`TypedDict` projection types the deep chain; iterating a generic `TypedDict`
type var still yields broad values — cast internally where needed.
